  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 350 AM EDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\n- Showers and Storms Once Again Today with Severe Potential\n\nShowers and thunderstorms continue to fill in to our west over\nLake Michigan and Wisconsin. This convection is occurring on the\nnose of the low level jet which is aiding in low level theta-e\nadvection into the storms. The low level jet is forecast, which\nwas discussed in yesterday afternoon's AFD, to fold over to the\neast and be aimed into Southwest Lower Michigan much of the\nmorning. Consistency with this feature has been good, which is\nsomething we have not seen of late in the models given somewhat\nnebulous forcing which is common in the late summer. Deep layer\nshear is expected to be around 40 knots this morning with MUCAPE\nvalues in the 1,000 to 2,000 j/kg range. The parameter space is\nrobust even at this early hour which is evidenced by nearly 2 inch\nhail in the middle of the night to the west of the lake in\nWisconsin. \n\nWe expect rounds of storms to move through Southwest Lower\nMichigan this morning between 4am and noon. The initial activity\nis crossing the lake now and given the surge of low level moisture\nvia the low level jet severe weather is possible any time during\nthat window. Its possible some activity may persist slightly past\nmidday in our south and east towards JXN and LAN, but the\nafternoon should trend drier with time. Wind looks to be the main\nsevere threat with gusts to 60+ mph possible. Severe hail cannot\nbe ruled out either. \n\nHeavy rain and localized flooding remain possible today given\nPWATs near 2.00 inches and the threat of training thunderstorms.\nAmounts of 0.50 to 1.00 inches of rain will be likely, but swaths\nof 1.50 to 3.00 inches are quite possible as well. Short term\nflooding potential will be monitored this morning.\n\nSome redevelopment of showers and storms in the far southwest CWA\ntowards South Haven will be possible this evening. \n\n- Period of Dry Weather This Weekend into Early Next Week\n\nA period of dry weather is expected this weekend into early next\nweek as ridging will be in control of the area weather. High\nconfidence in dry weather this period given consensus in the \nensembles of both the GFS and ECMWF. \n\n- Less Humid Air This Weekend\n\nAfter what has been a period of very humid air it will be\nnoticeably less humid this weekend. Dew points are in middle 60s \nto around 70 this morning. Dew points in the 50s this weekend will\nfeel quite pleasant in comparison.",
